    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d367-a1">

                <pb facs="0671" n="609" sameAs="frus:frus1878/pg609"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 1 in No. 785.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Foster to Mr. Mata.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Mexico</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1878-09-10"><hi rendition="#italic">September</hi> 10,
                        1878</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Haying communicated to the Secretary of
                    State at Washington a report of the conference which I had the honor to hold
                    with Your Excellency on the 21st, 24th, and 28th of June last, in regard to
                    affairs on the Rio Grande frontier, and having transmitted to him copies of your
                    note of July 12 last, and my reply thereto, concerning the crossing into Mexico
                    of American troops in the preceding month, I am now in receipt of his
                    acknowledgement thereof.</p>
                <p>The Secretary of State has been pleased to approve of my note addressed to Your
                    Excellency on the 15th of July, and has set forth the views of my government at
                    some length relating to frontier affairs. In order that Your Excellency may be
                    correctly informed of the position held by my government on this important
                    question, I inclose herewith a copy of the dispatch which the Secretary of State
                    has addressed to me on the subject.</p>
                <p>I improve the opportunity to reassure Your Excellency of my high consideration
                    and esteem.</p>
                <closer><signed>JOHN W. FOSTER.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
